    description: "Idea (owner-approved to file, 2026-11-10; not measured): instead of REMOVING tests from the local run (--narrow), ORDER them. Run first the tests the coverage index saw executing the changed blocks, then the citation-gate tests, then the rest of the selection. Nothing is dropped, so neither the whole-tree text readers (WI-zajuv measurement: 69 test files) nor import-time code (WI-zunug) can cause a miss, and the CI manifest is untouched.\n\nLimit, stated up front: a green run takes as long as today. The gain is time-to-first-failure only.\n\nOpen questions to measure before building: how pytest-xdist distributes an ordered list (ordering may be lost across workers); how often a failing local run's first failure is in the coverage-directed set (the smart-test bed, scripts/smart-test-bed, can score this: for each edit, the rank of the first MUST test).\n\nDone when: measured on the bed, and either shipped with the rank numbers or closed with the reason it does not help."  # 94ca
    fields: {}  # 94ca
